    "verseCount": 7,
    "content": "<p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"1\" data-sid=\"PSA 125:1\" class=\"v\">1</span>When the lord brought back the captivity of Sion, we became like men comforted.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"2\" data-sid=\"PSA 125:2\" class=\"v\">2</span>Then was our mouth filled with gladness; and our tongue with joy. Then shall they say among the Gentiles: The Lord hath done great things for them.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"3\" data-sid=\"PSA 125:3\" class=\"v\">3</span>The Lord hath done great things for us: we are become joyful.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"4\" data-sid=\"PSA 125:4\" class=\"v\">4</span>Turn again our captivity, O Lord, as a stream in the south.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"5\" data-sid=\"PSA 125:5\" class=\"v\">5</span>They that sow in tears shall reap in joy.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"6\" data-sid=\"PSA 125:6\" class=\"v\">6</span>Going they went and wept, casting their seeds.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"7\" data-sid=\"PSA 125:7\" class=\"v\">7</span>But coming they shall come with joyfulness, carrying their sheaves.</p>",
